{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Joseph and Rachel drew near.</b> With all of them, the mothers drew near ahead of the children — but with Rachel, Joseph drew near ahead of her. He said: My mother is fair of form; perhaps that wicked man will fix his eyes on her — I will stand in front of her and block him from looking at her. From this Joseph merited the blessing of 'over the eye.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:52.487194928Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}